# The Josephus problem: n people stand in a circle and every k-th is
# removed until one is left. Prints the order in which they go; the last
# number is the survivor.
#
# Cell 100 + i holds 1 once person i has gone.

π' → A
? → n
? → k
n → l               # l people are left
0 → i

π' → B              # While anyone is left, count k people who are still in.
k → c
(1 ∩ l)·C → π

π' → C              # Step to the next person, round the circle.
(i mod n) + 1 → i
100 + i → a
(1 ∸ ↓a)·D + (1 ∩ ↓a)·C → π

π' → D              # Still in: count them. The k-th goes.
c ∸ 1 → c
(1 ∩ c)·C + (1 ∸ c)·E → π

π' → E
1 → ↓a
i → ?
l ∸ 1 → l
B → π
